  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cross-River Women Business Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The relationship between Moldova and its break-away region Transnistria demarcated by the Dniester river is marked by ideological and geopolitical differences and characterised by social fragmentation and distrust. Women entrepreneurship can be a force for socio-economic good by enhancing social stability, promoting local community development and building connections across both banks of the river. However, women&#x2019;s entrepreneurship in the region is constrained by a combination of factors including socio-cultural stereotypes, limited entrepreneurial experience and lack of access to finance.By establishing a permanent cross-river online business support platform, the purpose of this project is to enable women entrepreneurs on the left bank of the Dniester river to develop their business activities across the right bank and to contribute to deeper trust and cooperation between communities on both sides of the Dniester river.</narrative>
  </description>
